  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved framework conditions for sustainable development</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="269636" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">SSC contributions in 2019 to framework conditions within maritime affairs in Ghana: &quot;3 &quot;.

Score from 1-5, 1 lowest and 5 highest.

The planned output targets in the project have generally been met in 2019.

The project continues to build ever-closer relations between Danish and Ghanaian stakeholders, and improves framework conditions for the Ghanaian maritime sector as the project moves on. Concretely, the framework conditions have been strengthened by improving cooperation on safety, e-navigation and IMO compliance. The SSC has thus created the foundation for favourable prerequisites for a free competition and an international maritime level playing field that benefits both Ghana and Denmark. Moreover, the project has also contributed to improved relations between Danish, Ghanaian and other west-African stakeholders outside of the concrete SSC project. In particular relating to the regional Maritime Security Programme concerning the Gulf of Guinea (MSP GoG).</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5"></target>
     <actual value="3"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
