  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Four tug boat captains have completed a tug boat handling course in Denmark.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="271009" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluation report on completed training.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Evaluation report on completed training."></target>
     <actual value="Due to covid19 it has not been possible to carry out the evaluation of the training programme physically in Ghana. Therefore the activity will be carried out online during Q1 2021."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Evaluation report on completed training."></target>
     <actual value="Ghana has improved the maritime safety in the Port of Tema through capacity development within training of tugboat masters in Denmark and the establishment of &#x201c;Tug Pilot Meetings&#x201d; (TPM) via virtual means due to Covid-19 travel restrictions. GPHA mentioned that procedures have been implemented for operating in bad weather and standing operating procedures for normal operations had been introduced. This had resulted in several concrete incidents being avoided due to the training and new procedures. Most importantly was the new procedure of always connecting tugboats to the target ship in &#x201c;open water&#x201d; before passing through the narrow breakwater to the terminals. Shortly after this procedure was introduced, via the SSC programme, a large container vessel had an engine failure whilst in a critical position close to the brake water. The tug boats were able to safely assist the vessel and avoid a potential environmental disaster and possible closure of the port had the vessel drifted aground"></actual>
    </period>
